WEBVTT

00:04:29.932 --> 00:04:33.352
That's why, for low-probability,
high-impact events,

00:04:33.394 --> 00:04:34.770
we share risk,

00:04:34.812 --> 00:04:37.231
and in some instances, like car insurance,

00:04:37.231 --> 00:04:38.524
we even require it.

00:04:38.941 --> 00:04:41.277
We could do the same thing
in supply chains.

00:04:41.277 --> 00:04:46.824
Industry players could team up to share
the cost of keeping extra raw materials,

00:04:46.824 --> 00:04:48.993
key components or even machinery,

00:04:49.035 --> 00:04:51.454
in exchange for an ongoing shared fee,

00:04:51.454 --> 00:04:54.457
and only to be used in times of a crisis.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:55.916
For example,

00:04:55.958 --> 00:04:58.544
many countries stockpile
important medicines,

00:04:58.544 --> 00:05:02.590
but relatively few keep
their active ingredients, or "APIs."